.\" Keep this page current: it describes the demo game demos/fruit2.bas (an executable made with BUILD, installed by "make install").
.TH ENGINE1999-FRUIT2 6 "November 2026" "Engine 1999 @VERSION@" "Engine1999 Manual"
.SH NAME
engine1999-fruit2 \- Fruit Invaders II, a gardener throws balls at marching fruit, with music
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B engine1999-fruit2
.SH DESCRIPTION
Fruit Invaders II is the middle edition of the fruit games: the game of Fruit Invaders with shaded, animated sprites, a sunny sky with a sun, hills and clouds that drift at three speeds, a gardener with a walking cycle who loses his hat when a seed hits him, a bird that flies by, music that gets faster with every wave, and more effects. Throw balls at the fruit before it reaches the bushes: cherries are worth 50 points, strawberries 40, apples 30, oranges 20, lemons 10, the bird 50 to 300. Now and then a banana falls out of a fruit: catch it with the gardener for rapid fire (two balls at a time). Seeds can be knocked out of the air with a ball. You have lives and get an extra life for every few thousand points. See also \fBengine1999-fruit\fR(6), the simple edition, and \fBengine1999-fruit3\fR(6), the biggest one.
.PP
The program is the demo \fIfruit2.bas\fR of Engine1999, made into an executable with
.B BUILD
(window kind: it needs the SDL2 library, nothing else); its BASIC libraries are inside it. It opens the Engine1999 window; the window can
be switched between the full screen and a window with F11 or ALT+RETURN.
.SH CONTROLS
.TP
.BR LEFT / RIGHT " or " A / D
walk (only while the key is held).
.TP
.BR SPACE " or " UP
throw a ball (hold it for rapid fire).
.TP
.B P
pause.
.TP
.B Q
quit.
.PP
A game controller works, too: D-pad or left stick walks, A or the right trigger throws, START pauses, BACK quits.
.SH FILES
The high score is kept in the file
.I fruit2.hi
in the folder
.IR ~/.local/share/fruit2/
(the driver
.BR local: ;
the file is safe there and needs no permission; a file of that name in the current directory, where older versions kept it, is still read when the new one does not exist yet; the game goes on without the file if it cannot be written).
.BR engine1999\-basic (7)
has the details, see FILES AND DEVICES.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR engine1999 (1),
.BR engine1999-basic (7),
.BR engine1999-fruit (6)
